For our experiments, we create an \textit{evaluation set} consisting of the three subsets: First, we choose a subset of audio recordings from the MAESTRO dataset that captures a wide range of musical repertoire and style in terms of composers and performers. Following this rationale, we select recordings from all (train, validation, and test) splits of the dataset as they are officially provided by the authors\cite{hawthorne2021sequence}. We make this latter choice by design, to test whether the split category would influence the generalization capability of the analysed models.\footnote{The official MAPS splits \cite{hawthorne2019enabling} ensure a unique piece-to-split mapping.} An overview of the selected MAESTRO subset is shown in Table \ref{tab:eval_dataset_table}.

